    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>A minor Spanish nobleman's son who bought an officer's commission for adventure in the New World, Francisco de Polonia distinguished himself on a doomed expedition into what is now New Mexico and was Embraced by @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.phgt6OMwTAoAaKfR]{Lasombra} elders as a deliberate stalking horse meant to draw out the region's Garou. He survived, trained for centuries under the legendary Medina, and rose to command all @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.6868ee8c357f4b73]{Sabbat} operations on the East Coast of North America &mdash; controlling Atlanta, northern Florida, the Carolinas, and most of the Mid-Atlantic even as the loss of New York to the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.fc464242d84d4e34]{Camarilla}'s 1999 counteroffensive shadows his reputation. Archbishop Polonia still commands the loyalty of @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.6868ee8c357f4b73]{Sabbat} remnants like Hester Reed's pack, Love's Easy Tears, and remains determined to retake the richest prize on the Eastern Seaboard.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Analyze before acting, trust your instincts, and let successes and failures alike roll off you like water &mdash; except New York, whose loss rankles you more than you admit. You would rather silence your second-guessers by winning the city back than waste energy on them directly. Any mention of the sunburn you were Embraced with breaks your iron composure instantly.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Anton de Concepcion. Embraced while suffering a severe sunburn; his reddened, imperfect complexion is his only vanity's flaw. Obtenebration 6 and other ratings above 5 from the original stat block have been capped to 5 for LARP play.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
